AWPTCM-T9554 (1.0) — MAC/Phy TLV: port speed=1000 duplex=auto
tb470 IE520 stack · port2.0.1 (member 2, AT-SP10TM copper SFP) · 2026-09-03

*** NOTE — THE EXPECTED AUTO-NEG RESULT IS INCORRECT AS WRITTEN ***
The case expects "Auto-neg Supported/Disabled". That is wrong for this configuration.
Forcing speed alone with duplex left auto (exactly what this case specifies) does NOT
disable auto-negotiation on AlliedWare Plus — the correct value is "Supported, Enabled".
Auto-neg only reads Disabled when BOTH speed and duplex are forced. Confirmed identical
across two platforms and two link partners: IE520 (this run) and a prior IE360/AR3050 run
both advertise Supported/Enabled at speed 1000, duplex auto. The advertised capability
([none]) and operational MAU type (1000BaseTFD) match as written — the testers verified
the MAU type and appear to have copy-pasted the autoneg line across the sheet.

  Corrected expected result:
    Auto-neg Supported/ENABLED, advertised capability none, operational MAU type 1000BaseTFD.

RESULT: PASS against the corrected expected result. CLI and MIB agree.
Full reasoning + the 3-config table: autoneg-mac-phy-clarification.txt

